<title>ITALY: ATHLETICS-TULU TAKES WOMEN'S WORLD CROSS COUNTRY TITLE.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-TULU TAKES WOMEN'S WORLD CROSS COUNTRY TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ethiopia's Derartu Tulu won the women's senior event run over 6.7 kms at the world cross country championships on Sunday in an unofficial time of 20 minutes and 53 seconds.</p>
<p>Paula Radcliffe of Britain finished second and Ethiopia's Gete Wami was third.</p>
